{%- comment -%}
  Cost reframe — the price, spread honestly over the nights it is guaranteed
  for: "£169 ÷ (5 years × 365 nights) = about 9p a night".

  Honest by construction:
    - the basis is the guarantee length from Theme settings, stated in full
      under the sum ("A way of seeing the cost, not a payment plan");
    - integer arithmetic, rounded half-up to the nearest penny, "about";
    - renders only when Theme settings → Pricing → per-night is on AND the
      guarantee is on with a length (the guarantee IS the basis). Otherwise
      it hides on the live store and explains why in the editor.

  Price source: a real bed, always. The chosen product's lowest price
  ("from"), else the product being viewed on a product page, else the first
  eligible bed in the store (an available one if there is one). The sum is
  "price ÷ the foam guarantee", so only a bed that guarantee covers can be
  used: snippets/foam-bed (title, type or tags mention orthopaedic / memory
  foam; a guarantee:yes / guarantee:no tag overrides that), the same test as
  the per-night line, mechanism and comparison sections. With no eligible bed (e.g. a store with no products yet,
  or a nest bed chosen) the section hides on the live store; the editor
  previews it with the example price setting and says why.

  Everyday comparisons (blocks) show how many nights on the bed the same
  money covers ("A takeaway coffee, about £3.50 ≈ 38 nights"). Keep them
  realistic; they are merchant copy.

  Text can use [per_night], [price], [guarantee_years], [product].
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign s = section.settings
  assign years = settings.guarantee_years | default: 0 | plus: 0
  assign settings_ok = false
  if settings.show_per_night and settings.guarantee_enable and years > 0
    assign settings_ok = true
  endif

  assign source_product = s.product
  if source_product == blank and template.name == 'product' and product != blank
    assign source_product = product
  endif

  assign source_ok = false
  if source_product != blank
    capture c_foam
      render 'foam-bed', product: source_product
    endcapture
    if c_foam == 'true'
      assign source_ok = true
    endif
  else
    comment
      Nothing chosen: the first eligible bed with a price, preferring one
      that can be bought today.
    endcomment
    assign first_ok = nil
    for p in collections.all.products limit: 50
      if p.price_min > 0
        capture c_foam
          render 'foam-bed', product: p
        endcapture
        if c_foam == 'true'
          if first_ok == nil
            assign first_ok = p
          endif
          if p.available
            assign first_ok = p
            break
          endif
        endif
      endif
    endfor
    if first_ok != nil
      assign source_product = first_ok
      assign source_ok = true
    endif
  endif

  assign cents = 0
  if source_ok
    assign cents = source_product.price_min | default: 0 | plus: 0
  endif
  assign enabled = false
  if settings_ok and source_ok and cents > 0
    assign enabled = true
  endif

  comment
    Editor preview only: with no eligible bed, the example price stands in
    so the section can be designed. It never reaches the live store.
  endcomment
  assign preview = false
  if enabled == false and settings_ok and request.design_mode
    assign example_cents = s.price | default: 0 | times: 100 | round | plus: 0
    if example_cents > 0
      assign cents = example_cents
      assign preview = true
    endif
  endif
-%}
{%- if enabled or request.design_mode -%}
{{ 'sections.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
{%- render 'section-styles', section: section -%}
{%- liquid
  assign heading_id = section.id | append: '-heading'
  assign show_sum = false
  if enabled or preview
    assign show_sum = true
  endif
  if show_sum
    assign nights = years | times: 365
    assign twice_nights = nights | times: 2
    assign rounded = cents | times: 2 | plus: nights | divided_by: twice_nights
    if rounded < 1
      assign rounded = 1
    endif
    assign hundredths = cents | times: 200 | plus: nights | divided_by: twice_nights
    assign whole = hundredths | divided_by: 100
    assign frac = hundredths | modulo: 100
    if frac < 10
      assign frac = '0' | append: frac
    endif
    if rounded < 100
      assign per_night = rounded | append: 'p'
      assign exact_text = whole | append: '.' | append: frac | append: 'p'
    else
      assign per_night = rounded | money
      assign exact_text = rounded | money
    endif
  else
    assign nights = 0
    assign per_night = ''
    assign exact_text = ''
  endif

  assign price_short = cents | money_without_trailing_zeros
  assign price_full = cents | money
  assign years_text = years | append: ''
  assign nights_text = nights | append: ''

  if enabled
    assign product_name = source_product.title | escape
    if source_product.price_varies
      assign price_label = 'home.cost.product_from' | t: product: product_name
    else
      assign price_label = product_name
    endif
  else
    assign product_name = ''
    assign price_label = 'home.cost.example_label' | t
  endif

  assign heading = s.heading | default: '' | escape | replace: '[per_night]', per_night | replace: '[price]', price_short | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_text | replace: '[product]', product_name
  assign body = s.body | replace: '[per_night]', per_night | replace: '[price]', price_short | replace: '[guarantee_years]', years_text | replace: '[product]', product_name

  comment
    Comparison items: nights on the bed the same money covers, and the
    largest figure for the bar scale.
  endcomment
  assign item_blocks = section.blocks | where: 'type', 'item'
  assign max_nights = 1
  for block in item_blocks
    assign ic = block.settings.price | default: 0 | times: 100 | round | plus: 0
    if ic > 0 and cents > 0
      assign covered = ic | times: nights | times: 2 | plus: cents | divided_by: cents | divided_by: 2
      if covered > max_nights
        assign max_nights = covered
      endif
    endif
  endfor

  assign finder_url = routes.root_url | append: '/pages/bed-finder' | replace: '//', '/'
  assign cta_label = s.cta_label | default: '' | strip | escape
  if cta_label == ''
    assign cta_label = settings.finder_cta_label | default: '' | strip | escape
  endif
  if cta_label == ''
    assign cta_label = 'home.hero.finder_cta' | t
  endif
-%}
<section
  class="section cost-reframe scheme-{{ s.color_scheme }}"
  id="{{ section.id }}-wrap"
  aria-labelledby="{{ heading_id }}"
>
  <div class="page-width">
    {%- if settings_ok == false -%}
      <p class="editor-note">{{ 'home.editor.cost_hidden' | t }}</p>
    {%- elsif enabled == false -%}
      <p class="editor-note">{{ 'home.editor.cost_example' | t }}</p>
    {%- endif -%}
    <div class="cost-reframe__inner">
      <div class="cost-reframe__copy">
        {%- if s.eyebrow != blank -%}<p class="eyebrow">{{ s.eyebrow | escape }}</p>{%- endif -%}
        <h2 id="{{ heading_id }}" class="h2">{{ heading | default: shop.name }}</h2>
        {%- if body != blank -%}<div class="rte cost-reframe__body">{{ body }}</div>{%- endif -%}
        {%- if s.cta != 'none' -%}
          <div class="cost-reframe__actions">
            {%- if s.cta == 'product' and enabled -%}
              <a class="btn btn--secondary" href="{{ source_product.url }}">
                <span>{{ 'home.cost.see_product' | t: product: product_name }}</span>{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right' -%}
              </a>
            {%- elsif settings.finder_enable -%}
              <a href="{{ finder_url }}" class="btn btn--secondary" data-open-finder aria-haspopup="dialog">
                <span>{{ cta_label }}</span>{%- render 'icon', name: 'arrow-right' -%}
              </a>
            {%- endif -%}
          </div>
        {%- endif -%}
      </div>

      {%- if show_sum -%}
        <div class="cost-reframe__panel" data-reveal>
          <p class="visually-hidden">
            {{- 'home.cost.sr_sum' | t: price: price_short, years: years_text, nights: nights_text, amount: per_night -}}
          </p>
          <div class="cost-reframe__sum" aria-hidden="true">
            <div class="cost-reframe__term">
              <span class="cost-reframe__value">{{ price_short }}</span>
              <span class="cost-reframe__label">{{ price_label }}</span>
            </div>
            <span class="cost-reframe__op">÷</span>
            <div class="cost-reframe__term">
              <span class="cost-reframe__value">{{ years }}<span class="cost-reframe__times">×</span>365</span>
              <span class="cost-reframe__label">{{ 'home.cost.nights_label' | t: years: years_text }}</span>
            </div>
            <span class="cost-reframe__op">=</span>
            <div class="cost-reframe__term cost-reframe__term--result">
              <span class="cost-reframe__value">{{ per_night }}</span>
              <span class="cost-reframe__label">{{ 'home.cost.a_night' | t }}</span>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p class="cost-reframe__basis">
            {{- 'home.cost.basis' | t: price: price_full, years: years_text, exact: exact_text -}}
          </p>

          {%- if item_blocks.size > 0 -%}
            <div class="cost-reframe__compare">
              {%- if s.compare_heading != blank -%}
                <h3 class="cost-reframe__compare-heading">{{ s.compare_heading | escape }}</h3>
              {%- endif -%}
              <ul class="cost-reframe__items" role="list">
                {%- for block in item_blocks -%}
                  {%- liquid
                    assign ic = block.settings.price | default: 0 | times: 100 | round | plus: 0
                    assign covered = 0
                    if ic > 0
                      assign covered = ic | times: nights | times: 2 | plus: cents | divided_by: cents | divided_by: 2
                    endif
                    assign pct = covered | times: 100 | divided_by: max_nights
                    if pct < 4
                      assign pct = 4
                    endif
                    if pct > 100
                      assign pct = 100
                    endif
                    assign item_price = ic | money_without_trailing_zeros
                  -%}
                  {%- if ic > 0 and block.settings.label != blank and covered > 0 -%}
                    <li class="cost-reframe__item" style="--pct: {{ pct }};" {{ block.shopify_attributes }}>
                      <span class="cost-reframe__item-label">
                        {{- block.settings.label | escape -}}
                        <span class="cost-reframe__item-price">{{ 'home.cost.about_price' | t: price: item_price }}</span>
                      </span>
                      <span class="cost-reframe__item-nights">{{ 'home.cost.covers_nights' | t: count: covered }}</span>
                      <span class="cost-reframe__bar" aria-hidden="true"><span class="cost-reframe__bar-fill"></span></span>
                    </li>
                  {%- endif -%}
                {%- endfor -%}
              </ul>
            </div>
          {%- endif -%}
        </div>
      {%- endif -%}
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
{%- endif -%}

{% schema %}
{
  "name": "Price per night",
  "disabled_on": { "groups": ["header", "footer"] },
  "max_blocks": 4,
  "settings": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Divides a price by the nights in your guarantee (Theme settings → Promises), rounded to the nearest penny, with the working shown. Hidden when per-night pricing or the guarantee is switched off. Text can use [per_night], [price], [guarantee_years] and [product]."
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "color_scheme",
      "label": "Colour scheme",
      "options": [
        { "value": "bone", "label": "Bone" },
        { "value": "oat", "label": "Oat" },
        { "value": "moss", "label": "Moss (dark)" },
        { "value": "white", "label": "White" }
      ],
      "default": "oat"
    },
    {
      "type": "product",
      "id": "product",
      "label": "Bed to price",
      "info": "Uses its lowest price. Leave blank to use the product being viewed on a product page, or else the first orthopaedic / memory foam bed in your store. A bed the foam guarantee doesn't cover (nothing in its title, type or tags says orthopaedic or memory foam, or it's tagged guarantee:no) hides the section."
    },
    {
      "type": "number",
      "id": "price",
      "label": "Example price (£)",
      "default": 169,
      "info": "Editor preview only: the live store always uses a real orthopaedic bed's price."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "eyebrow",
      "label": "Eyebrow",
      "default": "What it really costs"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "heading",
      "label": "Heading",
      "default": "About [per_night] a night."
    },
    {
      "type": "richtext",
      "id": "body",
      "label": "Text",
      "default": "<p>Dogs spend twelve to fourteen hours a day lying down. Spread over the [guarantee_years] years the foam is guaranteed for, a bed that actually holds them up works out at pennies a night.</p>"
    },
    {
      "type": "select",
      "id": "cta",
      "label": "Button",
      "options": [
        { "value": "finder", "label": "Open the Bed Finder" },
        { "value": "product", "label": "Go to the chosen bed" },
        { "value": "none", "label": "No button" }
      ],
      "default": "finder"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "cta_label",
      "label": "Bed Finder button label",
      "info": "Leave blank to use the label from Theme settings."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "id": "compare_heading",
      "label": "Comparison heading",
      "default": "The same money, elsewhere"
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_top",
      "label": "Top padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 72
    },
    {
      "type": "range",
      "id": "padding_bottom",
      "label": "Bottom padding",
      "min": 0,
      "max": 120,
      "step": 4,
      "unit": "px",
      "default": 72
    }
  ],
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "item",
      "name": "Everyday comparison",
      "settings": [
        {
          "type": "text",
          "id": "label",
          "label": "Item",
          "default": "A takeaway coffee"
        },
        {
          "type": "number",
          "id": "price",
          "label": "Typical price (£)",
          "default": 3.5,
          "info": "Keep it realistic. Shown as \"about £3.50\" with the nights on the bed it would cover."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "presets": [
    {
      "name": "Price per night",
      "blocks": [
        { "type": "item", "settings": { "label": "A takeaway coffee", "price": 3.5 } },
        { "type": "item", "settings": { "label": "A bag of dog treats", "price": 4 } },
        { "type": "item", "settings": { "label": "A cinema ticket", "price": 12 } }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
{% endschema %}
